  "description": "codeSpark: The Award-Winning Learn-to-Code App for Kids (Ages 3ΓÇô10)\n\n100s of coding games & activitiesΓÇöplus tools to create your own! Kids as young as 3 can start coding through play with puzzles, storytelling, and creativity tools designed just for them. Older kids can design and publish their own games, join monthly contests, and explore projects created by other kid coders.\n\nGet full access with a monthly or annual subscriptionΓÇötry membership free for 7 days! Annual subscribers can create up to 5 child profiles, making codeSpark perfect for families with multiple learners.\n\nOR play limited content through Hour of Code with no credit card required.\n\nLearn Coding Through Play\n - Puzzles ΓÇô Master core coding and problem-solving concepts level by level\n - Create ΓÇô Design and code your own games and interactive stories\n - Made by Kids ΓÇô Play and explore games created by other young coders around the world\n - Monthly Coding Contests ΓÇô Showcase creativity, code projects, and win prizes\n - Code Together ΓÇô Join friends in a multiplayer water balloon fight while practicing coding logic\n - Pre-Coding for Preschoolers ΓÇô Activities designed for early learners ages 3ΓÇô4\n - Adventure Maps ΓÇô Unlock new puzzles and challenges while progressing through fun coding worlds\n\nEducational Benefits Backed by Research\n codeSparkΓÇÖs curriculum is based on research from MIT, Princeton, and Carnegie Mellon. Kids learn the basics of computer science in a fun, accessible wayΓÇöwithout words.\n - Coding concepts: sequencing, loops, conditionals, events, and debugging\n - Computational thinking: problem-solving, logic, pattern recognition, and creativity\n - Reinforces early skills: reading, math, and critical thinking\n - Builds confidence, perseverance, and collaboration through play\n - Encourages design thinking by letting kids turn ideas into working games and stories\n\nKid-Safe & Ad-Free\n - Every game and story is reviewed before publishing to ensure safety\n - No ads, no micro-transactions, no distractions\n - Parent dashboard to manage profiles and track progress\n - A trusted environment for independent learning\n\nPraise from Parents & Teachers\n ΓÇ£My daughters are 6 and 8, and this is their new favorite game. Now they want to be programmers!ΓÇ¥ ΓÇô Parent Review\n \nΓÇ£I loved seeing how my children enjoyed working together on the puzzles.ΓÇ¥ ΓÇô Parent Review\n\nTeachers and parents worldwide use codeSpark to introduce coding in classrooms, after-school programs, and at home. Kids stay motivated because the learning feels like play, and they are proud to share their creations.\n\n - Awards & Recognition\n - The LEGO Foundation ΓÇô Pioneer in Reimagining Learning & Play\n - ChildrenΓÇÖs Technology Review ΓÇô EditorΓÇÖs Choice Award\n - ParentΓÇÖs Choice Award ΓÇô Gold Medal\n - Collision Conference ΓÇô Kids & Family Silver Winner\n\nWhy Families Choose codeSpark\n - Designed for kids ages 3ΓÇô10 with no reading required\n - Builds STEM skills through fun, engaging coding challenges\n - Supports creativity with open-ended game and story design tools\n - Encourages collaboration through multiplayer games and contests\n - Trusted by parents, teachers, and schools worldwide\n - Helps kids see themselves as creators, problem-solvers, and future innovators\n\nSubscription & Download\nStart with a 7-day free membership trial. Subscriptions renew automatically; manage or cancel anytime in Account Settings. Annual subscribers can create up to 5 child profiles, making it easy to support the whole family.\n\nPrivacy Policy: http://codespark.com/privacy/\nTerms of Use: http://codespark.com/terms/\n\nStart your childΓÇÖs coding journey today with codeSparkΓÇöthe award-winning learn-to-code app that makes programming fun, safe, and accessible for every kid ages 3ΓÇô10!",
